### Lot 5 step 3a demo, season passes and paid membership (IntelliJ HTTP client): plan lot-5 §11.1 Exit 3a (1)-(8)
### on one instance; Lot5PassesFlowTest runs the same flow in CI on a fixed clock.
#
# Start the backend with the dev profile on port 8080, so @base and the card redirect (PUBLIC_BASE_URL, dev default
# http://localhost:8080/v1) agree; the dev profile alone serves on 8090 (dev seed: ATLAS FC with a cash point,
# Admin Dev +212600000001, Caissier Dev +212600000002, Ops Dev +212600000003, Grand Stade with Tribune Est and Nord;
# the pass tickets job and the order expiry job run every 30 s; the simulated card gateway is on):
#   docker compose up -d && SERVER_PORT=8080 GATE_MANIFEST_LEAD=2400h SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun
# GATE_MANIFEST_LEAD: a scanner gets an event's manifest only from starts_at minus this lead (default 3h). The demo
# matches are in January and February 2027, so 2400h (100 days) lets the scanner load match 1 and admit a pass
# ticket offline (Exit 3a step 3) today; it changes nothing else.
# Every phone logs in with the dev OTP 123456 (JOMHOR_DEV_FIXED_OTP, dev default). The fan phones are made up.
# Card payments: open the response's redirect_url in a browser and click "Approuver" right away (8 min hold).
#
# Each run makes a new series, so passes start afresh. Creating the MEMBERSHIP product (2.2) makes ATLAS FC's
# membership paid: from then on every "Tarif membres" of the dev club needs paid_until (plan lot-5 Q189).
# A re-run needs new fan phones (Yazid's cotisation is paid to @validUntil: 7.2 would answer MEMBERSHIP_PAID).
# At the end, backend/loadtest/check.sql must print no rows:
#   docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U jomhor -d jomhor < loadtest/check.sql

@base = http://localhost:8080/v1
@org = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@venue = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000301
@opsPhone = +212600000003
@cashierPhone = +212600000002
@yazidPhone = +212611153001
@karimPhone = +212611153002
@salmaPhone = +212611153003
@omarPhone = +212611153004
@nadiaPhone = +212611153005
@hamzaPhone = +212611153006
@code = 123456
# 30 June 2027, end of day in Casablanca (UTC+1); both products close at noon that day.
@validUntil = 2027-06-30T22:59:59Z
@closeAt = 2027-06-30T12:00:00Z

### ---------- (1) B2: the series "Saison 2026-27", three matches, "Abonnés" in Tribune Est ----------

### 1.1 OPS (Ops Dev): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}"}

### 1.2 OPS: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("orgToken", response.body.token); %}

### 1.3 OPS: the Grand Stade zones (keeps Est and Nord)
GET {{base}}/org/venues/{{venue}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("estId", response.body.zones.find(z => z.code === "EST").id);
     client.global.set("nordId", response.body.zones.find(z => z.code === "NORD").id); %}

### 1.4 OPS: the series -> 201
POST {{base}}/org/series
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Saison 2026-27", "starts_on": "2026-08-01", "ends_on": "2027-06-30"}

> {% client.global.set("seriesId", response.body.id); %}

### 1.5 OPS: match 1 in the series (DRAFT)
POST {{base}}/org/events
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"venue_id": "{{venue}}", "event_type": "FOOTBALL_MATCH", "title": "ATLAS FC – Démo abonnés 1",
 "starts_at": "2027-01-10T19:00:00Z", "series_id": "{{seriesId}}", "metadata": {"opponent": "Démo 1"}}

> {% client.global.set("m1", response.body.id); %}

### 1.6 OPS: match 2 in the series (DRAFT)
POST {{base}}/org/events
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"venue_id": "{{venue}}", "event_type": "FOOTBALL_MATCH", "title": "ATLAS FC – Démo abonnés 2",
 "starts_at": "2027-01-24T19:00:00Z", "series_id": "{{seriesId}}", "metadata": {"opponent": "Démo 2"}}

> {% client.global.set("m2", response.body.id); %}

### 1.7 OPS: match 3 in the series (stays DRAFT until step 6)
POST {{base}}/org/events
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"venue_id": "{{venue}}", "event_type": "FOOTBALL_MATCH", "title": "ATLAS FC – Démo abonnés 3",
 "starts_at": "2027-02-07T19:00:00Z", "series_id": "{{seriesId}}", "metadata": {"opponent": "Démo 3"}}

> {% client.global.set("m3", response.body.id); %}

### 1.8 OPS: match 1 "Abonnés" in Tribune Est (Accès: Abonnés, 0 DH, quota 2)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m1}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{estId}}, "name": "Abonnés", "price_mad": 0, "quota": 2, "audience": "PASS"}

> {% client.global.set("abo1Id", response.body.id); %}

### 1.9 OPS: match 2 "Abonnés" (quota 2)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m2}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{estId}}, "name": "Abonnés", "price_mad": 0, "quota": 2, "audience": "PASS"}

### 1.10 OPS: match 3 "Abonnés" (quota 3: room for every pass once it is published)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m3}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{estId}}, "name": "Abonnés", "price_mad": 0, "quota": 3, "audience": "PASS"}

### 1.11 OPS: match 1 "Tarif membres" in Nord (Accès: Membres, 30 DH), for step 7
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m1}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{nordId}}, "name": "Tarif membres", "price_mad": 3000, "quota": 10, "audience": "MEMBERS"}

> {% client.global.set("membersId", response.body.id); %}

### 1.12 OPS: publish match 1 (DRAFT -> ON_SALE)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m1}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 1.13 OPS: publish match 2
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m2}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (2) B14: the pass and the cotisation, both on sale ----------

### 2.1 OPS: "Abonnement Tribune Est" (PASS, 1 500 DH, quota 3) -> 201
POST {{base}}/org/products
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"kind": "PASS", "name": "Abonnement Tribune Est", "price_mad": 150000, "quota": 3, "series_id": "{{seriesId}}",
 "zone_id": {{estId}}, "sales_close_at": "{{closeAt}}", "on_sale": true}

> {% client.global.set("passId", response.body.id); %}

### 2.2 OPS: "Carte membre 2026-27" (MEMBERSHIP, 200 DH, valid until 30 June 2027) -> 201 (B14 warns first)
POST {{base}}/org/products
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"kind": "MEMBERSHIP", "name": "Carte membre 2026-27", "price_mad": 20000, "valid_until": "{{validUntil}}",
 "sales_close_at": "{{closeAt}}", "on_sale": true}

> {% client.global.set("cardId", response.body.id); %}

### 2.3 W9 / screen 13: the club's passes (public) -> the pass, remaining 3, pass.events = matches 1 and 2
GET {{base}}/fan/products?organizer={{org}}&kind=PASS

### ---------- (3) Yazid, a free member, buys the pass by card ----------

### 3.1 Yazid: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{yazidPhone}}"}

### 3.2 Yazid: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{yazidPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("yazidToken", response.body.token); %}

### 3.3 Yazid joins the club for free -> 201 (200 if already a member)
PUT {{base}}/fan/me/membership
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organizer_id": "{{org}}", "marketing_push": false, "marketing_whatsapp": false}

### 3.4 Yazid orders the pass -> 201 RESERVED, total_mad 150000, pass_id
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{passId}}", "channel": "APP", "holder_name": "Yazid Aqel"}

> {% client.global.set("yazidOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 3.5 Yazid pays by card: open redirect_url in a browser and click "Approuver"
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{yazidOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CARD"}

### 3.6 Yazid's passes -> ACTIVE
GET {{base}}/fan/passes
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}

### 3.7 Yazid's tickets, within about 30 s -> matches 1 and 2, each with pass_id (the "Abonnement" chip); keeps the
### match 2 ticket for step 8: re-run until both tickets show. The scanner app, assigned to match 1, admits the
### match 1 one offline (its manifest is available now thanks to GATE_MANIFEST_LEAD, header).
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}

> {% client.global.set("yazidM2Ticket",
       response.body.tickets.find(t => t.event.id == client.global.get("m2") && t.pass_id)?.id); %}

### 3.8 A second pass of the series -> 409 PASS_HELD {pass_id, status: ACTIVE}
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{passId}}", "channel": "APP", "holder_name": "Yazid Aqel"}

### ---------- (4) Salma's order is left unpaid; Karim pays his by a cash code at the till ----------

### 4.1 Salma: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{salmaPhone}}"}

### 4.2 Salma: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{salmaPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("salmaToken", response.body.token); %}

### 4.3 Salma orders the pass and never pays -> 201 RESERVED; it expires 8 min later (step 5.1)
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{salmaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{passId}}", "channel": "APP", "holder_name": "Salma Tazi"}

### 4.4 Karim: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{karimPhone}}"}

### 4.5 Karim: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{karimPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("karimToken", response.body.token); %}

### 4.6 Karim orders the pass on the shop (W9) -> 201 RESERVED
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{passId}}", "channel": "WEB", "holder_name": "Karim Alaoui"}

> {% client.global.set("karimOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 4.7 Omar: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{omarPhone}}"}

### 4.8 Omar: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{omarPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("omarToken", response.body.token); %}

### 4.9 Omar orders the pass while Salma's order still holds a place (Yazid, Salma, Karim: 3 of 3) -> 409 SOLD_OUT
### {product_id}
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{omarToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{passId}}", "channel": "APP", "holder_name": "Omar Idrissi"}

### 4.10 Karim takes a cash code -> 200 {pay_code, reserved_until (24 h), amount_mad 150000}
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{karimOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CASH_AGENCY"}

> {% client.global.set("karimCode", response.body.pay_code); %}

### 4.11 Cashier (Caissier Dev): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}"}

### 4.12 Cashier: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("cashierToken", response.body.token); %}

### 4.13 Cashier: open the till -> 201 (200 with the one already open)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"label": "Guichet stade"}

### 4.14 B11: the code -> payable, event null, product {name: "Abonnement Tribune Est"}, places 1
GET {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{karimCode}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 4.15 B11: collect 1 500 DH -> 200 PAID, ticket_ids [] (the pass job issues them)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{karimCode}}/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount_mad": 150000}

### 4.16 Karim's tickets (W5), within about 30 s -> matches 1 and 2, with pass_id
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}

### ---------- (5) expiry and quota ----------

### 5.1 Once 8 min (plus up to 30 s) have passed since 4.3, Salma's order has expired -> remaining 1
GET {{base}}/fan/products/{{passId}}

### 5.2 Omar orders the pass again -> 201 RESERVED
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{omarToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{passId}}", "channel": "APP", "holder_name": "Omar Idrissi"}

> {% client.global.set("omarOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 5.3 Omar pays by card: open redirect_url in a browser and click "Approuver"
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{omarOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{omarToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CARD"}

### 5.4 B14, about 30 s later -> passes {pending 0, active 3}, revenue_mad 450000; matches 1 and 2: issued 2,
### expected 3, pass_remaining 0 ("2/3 émis", "Ajoute 1 place Abonnés en Tribune Est"); match 3 (DRAFT): issued 0
GET {{base}}/org/products/{{passId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 5.5 OPS raises match 1's "Abonnés" to 3 -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/org/events/{{m1}}/prices/{{abo1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quota": 3}

### 5.6 Omar's tickets, within about 30 s -> match 1, with pass_id
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{omarToken}}

### ---------- (6) OPS publishes match 3: every active pass gets its ticket ----------

### 6.1 OPS: publish match 3
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{m3}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 6.2 B14, about 30 s later -> issued 3, 2, 3
GET {{base}}/org/products/{{passId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (7) paid membership ----------

### 7.1 Yazid (free member) picks "Tarif membres" -> 409 MEMBERS_ONLY {paid_required: true}
POST {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id": {{m1}}, "channel": "APP", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{membersId}}", "qty": 1,
  "holders": [{"name": "Yazid Aqel"}]}]}

### 7.2 Yazid orders the cotisation -> 201 RESERVED, pass_id null
POST {{base}}/fan/product-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"product_id": "{{cardId}}", "channel": "APP", "holder_name": "Yazid Aqel"}

> {% client.global.set("cardOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 7.3 Yazid takes a cash code -> 200 {pay_code, amount_mad 20000}
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{cardOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CASH_AGENCY"}

> {% client.global.set("cardCode", response.body.pay_code); %}

### 7.4 B11: the code -> product {name: "Carte membre 2026-27"}, event null
GET {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{cardCode}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 7.5 B11: collect 200 DH -> 200 PAID
POST {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{cardCode}}/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount_mad": 20000}

### 7.6 Yazid's card -> member.paid_until = @validUntil ("À jour jusqu'au 30 juin 2027"), paid_required true
GET {{base}}/fan/me/membership?organizer={{org}}
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}

### 7.7 Yazid picks "Tarif membres" again -> 201 RESERVED, total_mad 3000
POST {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id": {{m1}}, "channel": "APP", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{membersId}}", "qty": 1,
  "holders": [{"name": "Yazid Aqel"}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("membersOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 7.8 Yazid pays by card: open redirect_url in a browser and click "Approuver"
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{membersOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CARD"}

### 7.9 Nadia: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{nadiaPhone}}"}

### 7.10 Nadia: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
